cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it together with the original data and model sources listed in the README."
title: "DrugPerturb: prespecified benchmarks for predicting transcriptional responses to held-out compounds"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sun
    given-names: Ningyu
version: 5.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
repository-code: "https://github.com/NingyuSUN/drugperturb"
url: "https://github.com/NingyuSUN/drugperturb"
license: MIT
abstract: "Compound-held-out benchmarks of transcriptional response prediction on sci-Plex3, OP3 and Tahoe-100M. Structure-based models (v1-v2) and the published single-cell models chemCPA and biolord (v3-v5) are compared with information-matched and vehicle-anchored simple baselines. Every version follows a protocol committed before any fit, and predictions are sealed before test truth is computed. Third-party data and model code retain their own terms."
keywords:
  - drug-discovery
  - perturbation-modeling
  - single-cell
  - chemCPA
  - biolord
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
